Expose upstream's memory key-value store on the lib default export

Why: a key-value provider of our own has to behave as upstream's memory store
does, and a shared suite proves it only by running the same cases against
that store, so the store must be constructible.
Upstream status: the package exports no key-value provider, and lib/kv has
type declarations only, so the bundle's webpack module 1557 (kv/kv_memory) is
reached through the lib default export (module 8568) and its public type in
client/index.d.ts. Nothing upstream needs the base class,
KVStorageProviderBase, at runtime: it never reads a provider's id and never
tests a provider's class, so the base is not exposed.
Removal condition: upstream exports KVStorageProviderMemory, then delete this
patch and import it from the public entry point.

Applies with "patch -p1" from the package root, after 0001.

